1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,000
One static site, one data pipeline, no server code.

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:08,000
A Vite–TypeScript app; the finder installs on the phone and runs with the radio off.

3
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:14,000
The pipeline is Python, geopandas and rasterio: WorldPop, Malaria Atlas travel time, WHO and OpenStreetMap facilities, ESA land cover, Google Open Buildings —

4
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:20,000
— snapped onto NexaSEE's ten-kilometre grid: 272 squares, 250 kilobytes.

5
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:25,000
On the phone, one model: Whisper tiny, 41 megabytes, in the browser via transformers.js and ONNX Runtime. It only transcribes.

6
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:30,000
A spelling-tolerant matcher over 444 place names, twelve fixed sentences

7
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:33,500
and a slot-filled slip do the rest:

8
00:00:33,500 --> 00:00:36,000
nothing on the phone can invent a fact.

9
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:40,000
Built in a weekend on NexaSEE's open-source geo-somalia map.

10
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:44,000
Google's building detector checks every listed facility and finds villages far from care.

11
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:47,500
A test pushes 5,593 questions through the matcher: zero wrong answers without a confirmation.

12
00:00:47,500 --> 00:00:50,000
CI runs it on every push.

13
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:58,000
Next: an SMS short code carries a clinic's question to a volunteer doctor and back; de-identified answers become an offline protocol library.
